WEBVTT

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:11.670
Sangvis's Intruder attempted to
lay a careful trap and buy time.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.260
"IntruderA Sangvis High-End Model."

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.260
Sangvis's Intruder attempted to
lay a careful trap and buy time.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.640
Gentiane, with help from M16,
who'd been working alone,

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.180
were able to put a stop
to Intruder's efforts.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.650
So try your best...

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.110
...to be entertaining.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.730
Fake data?

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.860
Master!

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.360
Your mission has changed
from distracting the enemy

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.990
to taking down Intruder,
the Sangvis Ringleader.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.830
Splendid!

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.750
I didn't think you'd find me this fast.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.630
Sorry. It's my job to
bring down the house.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.040
M16!

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.170
Now everybody's together, huh?

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.550
It's great to have comrades, huh?

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.970
Do you know how much I worried about you?

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.560
You could at least show me a smile.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.180
I'm back, M4.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.930
Welcome back.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.820
So, this is the spot.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.110
M4, confirm the coordinates.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.120
M4!

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.700
Okay! Confirming.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.370
You've been a little too relaxed since
M16 got back, don't you think?

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.630
N-No, that's not true.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.540
You can't space out like
this during combat.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.010
What's wrong?

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.510
When I look at what's around us, it makes
me feel a lot of different things.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.800
You mean Safehouse 3?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.600
That was the biggest spot of
trouble we've ever been in.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.230
We almost all went down.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.850
That's why it's so complicated for me.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.360
But you're the one who noticed
the coordinates in the mission logs

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.070
had been changed.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.650
And you're the one who
wanted to investigate it.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.570
You need to take responsibility.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:03.370
I know, but I never thought I'd come back.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:04.870
Don't worry.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:08.330
The commander's forces
will open the way for us.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:13.170
Even if we do run into Agent again,
it won't end up like it did last time.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:18.630
Agent... It's been months since then,
and there's no sign of her.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.180
What is she planning?

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.720
And I'm curious about what Intruder said,
about the "real show".

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.640
It doesn't matter!

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.940
As soon as the commander gives the order,
I'm ready to go kick some Sangvis butt!

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.150
Enough.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.860
It's time to stop talking,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.610
and get a move on.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.180
There.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.030
Storage, like we thought?

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.740
Yes. Old model, though.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.990
Use an external device to check it.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.820
It may be trapped.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.030
Yeah.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:53.160
They are in your house.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.500
They are in your car.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.420
They are in the skies.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:02.920
Now, they are coming for you.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.260
So it's just voice? Same as before.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.390
"They are in your house."

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.220
"They are in your car."

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.850
"They are in the skies."

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.350
"Now, they are coming for you."

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.940
What does that mean?
I don't get it at all!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.480
You don't need to.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.520
It's just a code.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.440
The question is what we can get
by playing with the audio file.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:26.990
A video file?

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:28.030
Yup.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:31.830
I spent a week and this was all I got.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.500
What is this?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:39.290
Records of AR15 at Safehouse 3, which
aren't accessible with my privileges.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.510
It contains a full record of
everything AR Team did there.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.880
But some of the angles show
they come from drones.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:51.180
That doesn't match with what we're
told about them being out there alone.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:54.930
But if this mission was that important,

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:58.230
it makes no sense that a
commander wasn't there.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:03.360
Unless there was a commander who
was hiding themselves for some reason.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.820
They'd know that M4 would
figure out the altered coordinates,

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:12.950
and in the end, reach this record.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.370
And this plan was built on

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.330
the assumption that AR Team would
break through the encirclement.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:25.050
So the person responsible knows
AR Team well and trusts their strength.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.840
So why was that memory
erased from their minds?

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.760
And why did the commander abandon them?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.220
I don't know.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.850
Dolls, humans, none of it makes any sense.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.110
Why did you hit me?

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:47.570
You seemed kind of down,
so my hand moved on its own.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.610
Sorry!

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:53.620
I don't know what
AR Team is thinking either,

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.120
but there's no need for them to
be doing anything they're doing.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:59.410
True.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:02.290
This isn't how AIs are supposed to behave.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:07.380
What's important is that they made
it possible for you to see this.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.050
It's a sign they trust you, isn't it?

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:19.430
This mysterious person may have wanted the
footage to go to someone they could trust.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.100
Trust?

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.270
It's been a long time since
I've heard that word.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.570
This world's got nothing left,

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:28.440
and I thought trust disappeared with
everything else a long time ago.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:33.160
I just remembered I've got
another business trip to go on.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.450
You mean that summons?

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.910
AR Team was called, too.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.580
They're going ahead of you.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.920
I wasn't told that!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.000
Persica wanted it to happen.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.090
Do you remember her? <i>That </i>Persica!

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.260
I don't want to hear that name!

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:53.550
Every time I get involved with her,
it means more work for me!

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.520
It was rough!

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:09.440
M4 was down all the time
till you got back, M16!

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.950
That's not true, I think.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:16.030
What? You weren't worried about me?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.370
That makes me sad.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:20.250
No, that's not what I meant!

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.710
What about me?

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.040
Same as ever.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.330
I see.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:29.460
Oh, AR15 is kind of hurt!

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.260
I'm not hurt!

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.580
You have reached the reception floor.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.210
Oh, Commander Gentiane!

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:17.010
I am the commander of
Base 737, Feodor Kamolov!

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:21.010
I was honored to fight by
your side the other day!

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:25.480
No, your team fought bravely
as well, Comrade Kamolov!

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.770
I'm Shi Jun.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:32.480
It's great to see you in the flesh.
You're a very attractive girl.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.570
So what are you doing here?

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.120
We don't know.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:45.120
We were told to bring a minimum bodyguard
force and participate in a conference.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.920
Same as me, then.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.750
You guys are here too, huh?

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.260
You were a huge help in the last mission!

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.130
I'm really grateful!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.760
I'm surprised.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:02.890
You remembered me?

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.060
You're PPK, right?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.140
And you're Super SASS!

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.900
You were the heroes of that mission.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.560
Of course I remember.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:16.440
The commanders here just complain
about how few capabilities we dolls have.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.070
Maybe they have weird tastes in dolls?

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.700
I don't understand what
you're saying at all.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.000
Welcome to Griffin's Top Secret base.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.790
I'm glad to see you're all here on time.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.670
Or a little early, actually.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:38.680
Kryuger is taking care of another matter,

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:42.640
so I'll tell you why you were summoned.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:46.310
We know the Sangvis are pursuinga
new plan, called Parapluie,

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:49.190
though we don't know what it is.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:51.810
Given what we know about
Sangvis activity patterns,

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:57.440
no matter what form it takes,
it will be a serious threat.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:04.410
So, we've summoned a few chosen commanders
to this secret HQ to discuss our plans.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:08.750
So we're the chosen commanders?

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:11.040
You're free to interpret it that way.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:16.500
While we're waiting for Kryuger, feel free
to use the command room to practice.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.510
There are next generation dolls here, too.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.800
Test the effectiveness of
your doll commanding

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.640
and help us update our database.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:28.390
If you find a doll you like,
you may request them.

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.060
We'll talk later.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.190
I'll pass.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:35.110
Me too.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.360
What?

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.530
This is the perfect chance to
check out new dolls up close!

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.700
You can't miss it!

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.740
I ran from the army 'cause I
didn't want to deal with that crap.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:48.330
And if it weren't for an
error in the information,

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:51.920
I would've just pretended I
never saw the Parapluie data.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:58.880
So that pain-in-the-ass audio data
got to Kalina from you, huh?

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:03.340
Do you know how long I spent
writing that report? Do you?

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.430
Um...

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:13.230
Commander Gentiane, would you like to use
this base's dolls to do a battle with me?

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:18.400
Actually, on social media, they say
you're the next big rookie star!

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.490
I'd love to see what you can do!

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.410
Yes, me too!

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.620
Fine.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:27.530
Yay!

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:28.990
Hooray!

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.200
"Two Hours Later"

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.790
"Two Hours Later"

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.790
Good work, everyone.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:38.710
I heard the rumors, but you really
are on a whole other level, huh?

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:42.260
You were giving perfectly accurate
orders to individual dummies!

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:45.590
And they were moving perfectly!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.010
Impressive!

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.930
How are you doing it?

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:53.020
Um, I talked to them a
little before the exercise.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.270
Talked to them?

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:58.230
One of them used to be an actress,

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.980
so I figured she'd be agile.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:04.360
And this one was originally
a security guard,

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.660
so I put her in an assault position.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.450
It worked out okay.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.870
And the others, I just played it by ear.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.000
I understand!

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:18.500
In other words, you talk to your dolls
and build a relationship with them!

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.920
That's fascinating!

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:24.380
PPK, tell me what you're best at.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.590
Oh my. Is it okay for me to show you here?

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:32.890
But if you insist, I will.

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:36.140
What was her old job?

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:38.650
I don't know, but I'm very jealous!

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.400
This is M4A1!

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.860
Commander, come in!

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:45.990
M4? What are you doing on this channel?

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.530
We got an order for an emergency mission.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:52.370
A large number of Sangvis have
appeared around the base!

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.910
M4, I guess it's a bad connection.
I can't hear you.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:57.120
Repeat that.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.380
Artillery?

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.000
That landed close!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.710
That's no firing exercise!

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:05.760
Commander, what was that noise?
Can you hear me, Commander?

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.010
Get down, everyone!

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.010
Commander Gentiane!

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.480
How many Sangvis are there?

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:19.810
An incredible number.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:21.480
I can't ID them all. There are too many!

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.530
Close every isolation gate.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:26.900
Seal off the destroyed
areas with phenolic resin.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:30.910
Commander Gentiane!

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.580
Wake up, new kid!

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.250
Do you know who I am?

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.920
I'm Kryuger, the top man at Griffin.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:42.460
You saw me on our company
newsletter plenty, right?

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.670
Can you still fight?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.380
I'm fine.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.550
We were hit with a surprise attack.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:52.260
First, protect yourself.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:53.850
Thank you.

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.350
There's a gun I'm used to using.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:00.940
Good, looks like you're ready for a fight.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.400
There are a lot of them,

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:07.690
so I've given command of the dolls
here to you and your co-workers.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:12.070
Stop their offensive and secure the base.

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:13.320
Understood.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:15.540
Medics, treat the wounded!

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:16.540
Open the door!

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.160
Bring up more ammo!

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.210
Where are the other commanders?

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:23.130
This is the supply room
at the bottom of the base.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.000
Everyone who can fight,
both dolls and humans,

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.050
are up at the top level
protecting the base.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:31.380
If you're joining the battle,
you'll need this.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:39.060
I never thought I'd be on the front lines.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.150
This isn't my job.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.810
Mobile Operations
Command System activated.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:48.740
Initiating combat data share
with local commanders.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.110
What's the situation, everyone?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.870
Commander Gentiane, you're safe!

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:56.910
The roof took a hit from some
kind of mystery weapon,

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:00.660
and 35% of our defense
systems are offline!

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:06.500
Sangvis are heading in from the hole
and heading for the upper levels!

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.840
The warning systems didn't pick them up?

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:14.890
The jamming destabilized the scan
system and outside communications!

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:19.310
We're lucky we could use a
closed channel in the base.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:22.100
Otherwise, it would've been really bad.

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.900
I think it's bad enough now.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:31.320
Um, Commander... Kawasaki?

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.660
You're too far ahead!

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.950
I don't want to be!

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.830
These are the front lines!

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.040
I see.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:45.380
There are too many of them!
We're being pushed back!

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.460
We're not going to last!

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:53.380
And the plan to seal the hole with
phenolic resin isn't going to work!

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:57.800
The Sangvis are using heavy
weapons that can destroy the resin!

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:03.230
Use it on the buildings.
It'll buy us a little time.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.770
Not a bad plan!

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:07.860
Let's all fall back to the
training exercise area!

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.070
Loading complete.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.150
Resin can be used on
the buildings at any time.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:14.030
Okay, falling back. Back me up!

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.320
Retreat!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.830
Retreat! Hurry!

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.660
We can buy time, but we can't
do anything about their numbers.

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:27.130
I want to help, but are
there any teams left?

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:30.340
Commander Gentiane! Commander Gentiane!

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.460
M4!

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.300
Good! We finally got through!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.720
M4, what's your status?

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.100
There are still a lot of enemies outside.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.720
We're looking for a way
past them and into the base.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:45.850
Outside? M4, wait!

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:48.520
Don't come back to the base!

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:49.650
But Commander...

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:52.980
Kryuger, give me permission

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:57.530
to send all dolls outside to find
and destroy the Sangvis base!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:02.080
This is an emergency, and the dolls
outside don't have commanders.

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:08.290
So you want AR Team to use their commander
modules to command the dolls?

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.250
Yes.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:12.170
Commander Gentiane,

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:15.510
the Sangvis are interfering with
our external communications.

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:17.340
Which means if they move
away from the base,

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:21.720
we'll have no means of
controlling them at all.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:26.020
Don't you think it's too dangerous?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:34.400
Unless we destroy that Sangvis base,
the enemy won't stop coming.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:40.200
Sending the teams outside back
here is telling them to die with us.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:46.000
And you think they have command ability?

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.250
I've seen them in action for months.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:51.210
I believe they'll be just fine!

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:57.720
On the battlefield, relying too much on a
relationship of trust can get you killed.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:02.220
But sometimes, you have to anyway.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:06.520
Do this your way then, rookie!

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.060
Right!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.020
AR Team, I'm changing your priorities.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:14.400
Devote your full efforts to finding
and destroying the Sangvis base!

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.570
But Commander!

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:17.530
M4!

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:19.280
I'm counting on you.

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:24.580
Roger.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:29.370
The teams outside have gone.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:32.210
Let's play with the enemy
on the training grounds.

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:36.800
So our fates are now
in the hands of dolls?

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.550
Are you insane?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:41.470
This is the way with the
best chance of survival.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:44.180
If you've got a better one, tell me.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.890
I don't, actually.

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:51.690
Shit.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:57.780
I gave you command priority.
What do we do, AR Team?

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:02.200
We split into three teams,
and fan out to search.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.370
Avoid combat as much as possible.

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:05.870
Will we make it?

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.330
There's too much ground to cover.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:09.540
That way.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:15.290
Vector EX3V25.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:21.130
Earlier recon showed 90% of
Sangvis coming from that direction.

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:25.180
If we head that way,
we'll very likely run into them.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.600
I guess that's why you're
the elite product.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.020
You think fast.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:30.680
Then we need to hurry.

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:34.520
Let's follow right behind AR Team.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:39.650
Thanks, AR15.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:42.280
I can't believe you found
their location so fast.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:48.660
I just want to finish this
mission as soon as possible.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.620
There's no time to talk.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:51.960
Let's go.

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:57.840
New Sangvis coming from heading 3-0-0.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.960
Handle them, AUG!

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.300
Roger.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:05.680
Is AR Team not done yet?

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:08.430
Long-range comms are jammed!

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:11.980
If the Sangvis stop moving,
that means it worked!

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.020
And if they don't?

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:17.400
I don't mean to rush you, but the
supply stockpiles are behind us!

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:19.230
There's nowhere to retreat!

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:20.400
Comrades!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:24.240
I'm honored to meet my end with you!

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:26.360
Shut up!

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:28.160
Target point reached.

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:31.370
Look! Around that abandoned building!

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.120
So many!

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:36.170
So this was their base!

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:38.080
The commander was right.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.790
There are too many.

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:42.710
If we'd gone back instead of
trying to destroy this base,

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:44.550
we would've been worn down and lost.

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:48.300
But how do we fight so many?

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.560
We've got a lot with us, too!

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.640
Don't be stupid.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:57.190
The Sangvis didn't think this
place would be attacked.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:21:59.690
The security is full of holes.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:02.780
I shared the enemy
locations with everyone.

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.820
Look, that area's open.

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:07.320
You're right!

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.530
We'll head in alone.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:12.790
Everyone else, protect this route.

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:16.790
If we're not back in five minutes,
blast the building.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.050
There's a place where
comms are concentrated.

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:26.470
This is going great!

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:28.890
Good job, AR15!

00:22:28.890 --> 00:22:32.850
I just got the recon done
while you were babbling.

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:35.890
We're going in.

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:47.570
Not this again.

00:22:47.570 --> 00:22:51.160
Quiet! Watch your surroundings!

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:52.490
No unusual signals.

00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:54.620
Clear.

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:56.750
Look at the footsteps.

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:59.620
The Ringleader here
probably just retreated.

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:03.040
Three minutes ago, to be exact.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:09.930
I am the Sangvis Ferri T-Doll, Destroyer!

00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:46.520
Episode 9: "The Kindling 02."
